\begin_layout Subsection
Evaluating attrition levels
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Evaluating-attrition-levels"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section we analyze attrition between baseline and endline to determine
 whether it is correlated with treatment status.
 Note that the analyses to follow exclude pure control households, as they
 were only surveyed at endline.
 First, we define the dummy variable 
\begin_inset Formula $attrit_{vh}$
\end_inset

 that indicates whether household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 was surveyed at baseline but not at endline.
 We then calculate overall attrition by treatment group.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Attrition1"

\end_inset

 we assess whether the probability of attrition is different for treatment
 and control households:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
attrit_{vh}=\alpha_{v}+\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}T_{vh}+\varepsilon_{vh}
\]

\end_inset

Second, in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Attrition2"

\end_inset

 we assess whether attrition households are different in terms of baseline
 values of our primary outcome variables: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
y_{vhB}=\alpha_{v}+\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}attrit_{vh}+\varepsilon_{vhB}
\]

\end_inset

Third, in Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Attrition3"

\end_inset

, we evaluate whether the baseline characteristics of attrition households
 in the treatment group are significantly different from those in the control
 group.
 The sample for this regression is restricted to attrition households: 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\left(y_{vhB}\mid attrit_{vh}=1\right)=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}T_{vh}+\varepsilon_{vhB}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In all analyses, standard errors are clustered at the household level.
 
\end_layout

