\begin_layout Subsection
Transfer and survey timing by treatment status
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We test whether treatment status predicts when a household completed endline
 using the following specification: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
SM_{vhi}^{E}=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}T_{vh}+\beta_{2}Sp_{vh}+\varepsilon_{vhi}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $SM_{vhi}^{E}$
\end_inset

 is the number of months from the date that the first endline survey was
 conducted to the date for which the endline survey was administered to
 individual 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 (omitted for measures from the household survey) in household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 in village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $Sp_{vh}$
\end_inset

 is a dummy for the spillover group.
 Standard errors are clustered at the village level when making comparisons
 across villages and at the household level otherwise.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta_{1}$
\end_inset

 captures the difference between treatment and pure control households in
 survey month date.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta_{2}$
\end_inset

 captures the difference in endline month between spillover and pure control
 households.
 Results are presented below.
 
