name "sec:Evaluating-Metal-Roof"

\end_inset

Evaluating Metal Roof Household Characteristics 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Baseline Balance on Immutable Characteristics
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "subsec:Baseline-Balance-on-immutables"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
One source of evidence for the comparability of the spillover and pure control
 samples is to compare them on baseline characteristics.
 However, no baseline survey was administered to pure control households.
 Nevertheless, there some individual and household characteristics are either
 immutable or calculable from endline values.
 We determine whether these characteristics are balanced between spillover
 and pure control households using the following specification:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
y_{vhiB}=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}Sp_{vh}+\varepsilon_{vhiB}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here, 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{vhiB}$
\end_inset

 is a characteristic of respondent 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 (if measured at the individual level) in household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 in village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 at baseline 
\begin_inset Formula $(t=B)$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $Sp_{vh}$
\end_inset

 is an indicator variable taking the value of 1 if household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 is a spillover household and 
\begin_inset Formula $0$
\end_inset

 if it is a pure control household.
 Note that we will exclude treatment households from this analysis.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon_{vhiB}$
\end_inset

 is an idiosyncratic error term.
 Standard errors are clustered at the village level.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta_{1}$
\end_inset

 identifies differences in immutable characteristics between spillover and
 pure control households.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We use the following characteristics as comparison variables: 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Age of primary respondent
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Marital status of primary respondent at baseline 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Highest level of education attained by primary respondent
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Number of children, excluding those born between baseline and endline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Household size at baseline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Results are presented below.
\end_layout

