\begin_layout Section
Within-village Spillovers
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this analysis, we exploit differences in the treatment intensity across
 villages, resulting from variation in the proportion of large vs.
 small transfers, to further examine the possibility of within-village spillover
s.
 We calculate the change in the mean wealth of the eligible households in
 each village as follows: 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\triangle\bar{T}_{v}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{H}\triangle T_{vh}}{H_{v}}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here, 
\begin_inset Formula $\triangle T_{vh}$
\end_inset

 is the assigned transfer amount for household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 in village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 (taking a value of USD 0, USD 404, or USD 1525), and 
\begin_inset Formula $H_{v}$
\end_inset

 is the total number of eligible households (those assigned to either treatment
 or control conditions) in village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

.
 We divide levels by 100 so that all results are per USD 100 increase in
 village mean wealth.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Restricting the sample to spillover households, we then analyze 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{equation}
y_{vhiE}=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}\triangle\bar{T}_{v}+\delta y_{vhiB}+\varepsilon_{vhiE}\label{eq:within-village_spillovers}
\end{equation}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
where 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{vhiE}$
\end_inset

 is the outcome of interest for individual 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 (where index 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 is excluded for measures taken at the household level) in household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 in village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 taken at endline 
\begin_inset Formula $(t=E)$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\triangle\bar{T}_{v}$
\end_inset

 is the change in village mean wealth.
 We condition on baseline values of outcome variables 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{vhiB}$
\end_inset

 where available.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon_{vhiE}$
\end_inset

 is an idiosyncratic error term.
 Standard errors are clustered at the village level since we exploit village-lev
el variation to identify these effects.
 Thus, 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta_{1}$
\end_inset

 identifies the effect of a USD 100 increase in the mean wealth of a village
 on the outcome of interest at endline among spillover households.
 Results are reported below.
 
\end_layout

