\begin_layout Section
Assessing the validity of measures of psychological wellbeing
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Psych_Predictors"

\end_inset

Predictors of psychological wellbeing and cortisol
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section we report the relationships i.
 between our psychological wellbeing index and each of our other seven outcome
 indices (Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:psy_index_z_indstems"

\end_inset

), and ii.
 between cortisol levels and each of nine measures of psychological wellbeing
 (Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:psy_index_z_indstems-1"

\end_inset

).
 We analyze both relationships both contemporaneously and across time.
 For each of the contemporaneous analyses, we report the following specification
: 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\Psi_{vhit}=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}y_{vhit}+X_{vhit}\mathbf{\delta}+\alpha_{v}+\varepsilon_{vhit}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
where 
\begin_inset Formula $\Psi_{vhit}$
\end_inset

 is alternatively our psychological wellbeing index or log cortisol levels
 for individual 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 in household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 of village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 at time 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 where 
\begin_inset Formula $t=\mbox{baseline or \ensuremath{t=\mbox{endline}}}$
\end_inset

.
 Note that this analysis includes all treatment, spillover and pure control
 households but that pure control households are only observed at 
\begin_inset Formula $t=\mbox{endline}$
\end_inset

.
 In the analysis of the psychological wellbeing index, 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{vhit}$
\end_inset

 is one of the seven other outcome variables (in 7 separate regressions),
 where the index 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 is excluded for outcomes measured at the household level.
 In the cortisol analysis, 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{vhit}$
\end_inset

 is one of nine self-reported measures of psychological wellbeing (in 9
 separate regressions), all measured at the individual level.
 
\begin_inset Formula $X_{vhit}$
\end_inset

 is a vector of individual level covariates including age, sex, education
 level, and marital status.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha_{v}$
\end_inset

 denotes village-level fixed effects.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon_{vhiE}$
\end_inset

 is an idiosyncratic error term.
 Thus 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta_{1}$
\end_inset

 identifies i.
 the contemporaneous relationship between the psychological wellbeing index
 and each of the 7 of other outcome indices in turn (reported in each of
 the 7 columns of row one of table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:psy_index_z_indstems"

\end_inset

 below), or ii.
 between log cortisol levels and the 9 measures of self-reported psychological
 wellbeing (reported in each of the 9 columns of row one of table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:psy_index_z_indstems-1"

\end_inset

 below) .
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To determine the relationship between these variables across time, we analyze
 the follow specification:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\Psi_{vhiE}=\beta_{0}+\beta_{1}y_{vhiB}+X_{vhiE}\mathbf{\delta}+\alpha_{v}+\varepsilon_{vhiE}
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
where 
\begin_inset Formula $\Psi_{vhiE}$
\end_inset

 is either our psychological wellbeing index or log cortisol levels for
 individual 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 in household 
\begin_inset Formula $h$
\end_inset

 of village 
\begin_inset Formula $v$
\end_inset

 at time 
\begin_inset Formula $\ensuremath{t=\mbox{endline}}$
\end_inset

.
 Note that this analysis excludes pure control household because they were
 not observed at baseline.
 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{vhiB}$
\end_inset

 is one of the seven other outcome variables at at time 
\begin_inset Formula $t=\mbox{baseline}$
\end_inset

, where the index 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 is excluded for outcomes measured at the household level.
 Thus 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta_{1}$
\end_inset

 identifies i.
 the inter-temporal relationship between the psychological wellbeing index
 and each of the 7 of other outcome indices in turn (reported in each of
 the 7 columns of row two of table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:psy_index_z_indstems"

\end_inset

 below), and ii.
 between log cortisol levels and the 9 measures of self-reported psychological
 wellbeing (reported in each of the 9 columns of row two of table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:psy_index_z_indstems-1"

\end_inset

 below).
 
\end_layout

