\begin_layout Subsection
Cronbach's alpha for psychological scales
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section, we report the internal consistency of the psychological
 scales used in the questionnaire.
 Specifically, Table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "tab:Cronbach's"

\end_inset

 reports Cronbach's alpha for each psychological measure that consisted
 of more than one question.
 We use the following formula:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\alpha=\frac{K}{K+1}\left(1-\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sigma_{Y_{i}}^{2}}{\sigma_{X}^{2}}\right)
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here, 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{X}^{2}$
\end_inset

 is the variance of the composite score (taken across all components), and
 
\begin_inset Formula $\sigma_{Y_{i}}^{2}$
\end_inset

 is the variance of component 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset Formula $K$
\end_inset

 is the number of observations.
 Note that we report this value for male and female subpopulations separately.
 
\end_layout

