 in a given column after joint-estimation using SUR.
 Columns (7) and (8) report the lower and upper Lee effect-size bounds adjusting
 for differential attrition generated by restricting to thatched roof households.
 This attrition is due to the higher rate of upgrade to metal roofs among
 spillover households and represents approximately 5 households or 10 individual
s.
 Columns (9) and (10) report lower and upper Manski-Horowitz bounds, imputing
 outcomes for the 5 attriting households using he 95th and 5th percentile
 of observed outcomes resepectively.
 In columns (1) through (4), standard errors clustered at the village level
 are reported in parentheses.
 In columns (7) through (10), bootstrapped standard errors are reported
 in parentheses.
 * denotes significance at 10 pct., ** at 5 pct., and *** at 1 pct.
 level.
